        "marks": 1,
        "mark_note": "Identity",
        "lines": [
          "The digestive system of the cockroach has two",
          "parts — the alimentary canal and the",
          "digestive glands.",
          "The alimentary canal runs from mouth to anus.",
          "It has three regions: foregut (stomodaeum),",
          "midgut (mesenteron) and hindgut",
          "(proctodaeum)."
        ],
        "why": "The three regions are the plan of the whole answer, so naming them first tells the examiner the order the description will follow and stops parts being written out of place.",
        "common_mistakes": [
          "Writing only the alimentary canal. The digestive glands are the second part and carry their own mark.",
          "Mixing the region names up. Foregut = stomodaeum, midgut = mesenteron, hindgut = proctodaeum."
        ],
        "memory_tip": "Fore, mid, hind: stomodaeum, mesenteron, proctodaeum — front to back, in that order.",
        "margin_note": "Two parts and the three regions, with both names for each region. Four short lines are enough."
